2.984,[[19,0.918,4,152],[13,0.082,12,13]],[["3058d447_3f3df294",22,-16,1,"Why not `span()`? https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:net/base/io_buffer.h;l=104;drc=c88d056b850747d4cae5e9e24222491efd85faf4"],["3d05e1d0_ae67b723",22,-16,1,"maybe base::as_writable_byte_span?"],["70f36dbb_70757044",22,-16,1,"Is this log intended?"],["0944397f_de0b21f1",23,-14,1,"Could you leave some comments to explain how this checksum is calculated, what the data source is, and when it is used?"],["13f6507f_7415b7d5",22,-14,1,"How often do we expect `owner_` and `owner_->sha256_checksum_` to be present vs missing? If they're often missing, it might be worth punting the `hasher->Update` calls. Then again, hashing is…"],["3ded0170_139f8286",22,-14,1,"This is already a byte span. `base::as_bytes` is only needed when you have a different type. ```suggestion hasher_->Update(buffer->span()); ```"],["7087270d_ca47d843",22,-14,1,"Optional: you can save an allocation by instead doing: ``` std::array<uint8_t, crypto::hash::kSha256Size> calculated_checksum; hasher_->Finish(calculated_checksum); bool checksums_match =…"],["9c67bb15_a447d898",22,-14,1,"See the note in the header: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:crypto/secure_hash.h;l=5-6"],["baa5056d_5ec1e129",22,-14,1,"The new `//crypto` APIs were designed to avoid needing to indirect to the heap when you don't need it. That seems to be the case here. So I think you can just write: ``` crypto::hash::Hasher…"],["df73e362_8ae55e6f",22,-14,1,"This looks like there may be a bug. I see this function both returns `buffer` *and* `read_bytes`. Are you sure you don't need to hash `buffer->first(read_bytes)` instead? Looking at `OnWritable`, I…"],["e68d0203_f805066b",22,-14,1,"Looks like `crypto::hash::kSha256Size` is the preferred spelling now? That then avoids the need for `crypto/sha2.h`."],["b1ab7de0_578af92a",22,-7,0,"The code looks not updated as discussed in https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7130007/comment/df73e362_8ae55e6f/ ?"],["75b45f4f_ad4ac324",22,6,0,"I'm not sure I fully understand, but is ServiceWorkerResourceRecord sometimes stored in stream 2 (kResponseMetadataIndex) of the disk cache? My understanding was that this was used for storing…"],["e9147d39_d2234bfa",22,6,0,"FWIW, it is perfectly safe to call `buffer->first(0)` and to pass an empty span to `hasher_.Update()`, so no need for this conditional. If `read_bytes` were negative, that'd be a problem, but you've…"]],0,947],[7259534,20437,629,0.056,0.024,[[35,0.605,0,389],[2,0.217,33,142],[36,0.06,0,36],[37,0.047,140,28],[38,0.038,0,23],[39,0.018,0,11],[12,0.017,307,10]],[],0,948],[7257931,20437,5,0.224,0.147,[[0,49]],[],0,948],[7259591,20437,4,0.248,0.178,[[40,0]],[],0,949],[7259815,20437,5,0.248,0.178,[[41,0]],[],0,950],[7258952,20437,8,0.407,0.29,[[12,307]],[],0,951],[7259007,20437,15,0.354,0.243,[[0,50]],[],0,952]]}